test_platforms_20261124.py named below were written by this author alone, who licenses them here, as their copyright
holder, under Apache-2.0; cryptovalid-opencore itself stays AGPL-3.0-or-later. ap2-evidence-pack and aee-verifier are
Apache-2.0. On 2026-11-25 cryptovalid 0.29.0 and ap2-evidence-pack 1.11.0 are not released: their commits named below
are in their public repositories, reachable by hash, on branches that are not the default one.

- nucleo/programs.py  which_absolute: cryptovalid (cryptovalid-opencore), 0.29.0 in preparation, commit f7883c9,
                      verifier.py `which`.
- nucleo/files.py     create_exclusive / create_private / private_tmpdir: cryptovalid commit 809be6a (unchanged in
                      f7883c9), verifier.py `create_private` and `owner_only`; ap2-evidence-pack commits df398fa and
                      5df7cb4, ap2_evidence.py `_create_exclusive` and `_private_tmpdir`.
- nucleo/jsonio.py    json_loads_bounded / json_nesting_depth / _RecursionHeadroom: cryptovalid commit f7883c9,
                      verifier.py (SPEC §30).
- nucleo/canonical.py canonical_json_jcs: aee-verifier commit 0d8cee1, aee_verifier/jcs.py (Apache-2.0).
- tests/test_vectors_rfc8785.py reads the vectors of RFC 8785 (A. Rundgren, B. Jordan, S. Erdtman, 2020, IETF Trust)
                      at test time from the official text named by NUCLEO_RFC8785; no vector, table or sample of the
                      RFC is kept in this repository: the test finds them by three short phrases of that text, and
                      DIFFERENZE.md cites one pair of numbers (Independent Submission stream: TLP 5.0 sections 3.c
                      and 4 do not apply, §8).
- tests/test_programs.py, tests/test_files.py: cases adapted from cryptovalid test_platforms_20261124.py (f7883c9,
                      classes NeverTheProgramOfTheCurrentFolder and TemporaryNamesOnWindows; there AGPL-3.0-or-later,
                      here Apache-2.0 by the same author). tests/test_canonical.py: unit cases from aee-verifier
                      tests/test_units.py (0d8cee1, Apache-2.0).

Where the sources differ from what is here, DIFFERENZE.md names each change and why.
